{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00479",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.94,
      "end_seconds": 3.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Evening. Long day, I imagine. Sit down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.92,
      "end_seconds": 5.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.13,
      "end_seconds": 8.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Did you find the place alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.74,
      "end_seconds": 13.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Yes, it was easy enough. The parking was the hard part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.1,
      "end_seconds": 16.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "What made you decide to come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.67,
      "end_seconds": 23.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "I've been dealing with more breathlessness than usual."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.52,
      "end_seconds": 26.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.76,
      "end_seconds": 32.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "Ever since... since Friday, really. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.22,
      "end_seconds": 35.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "How often does it happen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.24,
      "end_seconds": 37.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Honestly, all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.26,
      "end_seconds": 43.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.86,
      "end_seconds": 52.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.7,
      "text": "I mean, when it starts I tend to get a wheeze as well. The wheeze? That's been since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.77,
      "end_seconds": 55.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Mm-hm. Have you had any confusion or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.12,
      "end_seconds": 57.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "No, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.02,
      "end_seconds": 71.3,
      "duration_seconds": 13.28,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.62,
      "end_seconds": 73.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.99,
      "end_seconds": 79.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.6,
      "end_seconds": 82.52,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "Nothing, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.24,
      "end_seconds": 87.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.68,
      "end_seconds": 88.38,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.91,
      "end_seconds": 108.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.22,
      "end_seconds": 111.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "No, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.94,
      "end_seconds": 116.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.49,
      "end_seconds": 121.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.74,
      "end_seconds": 126.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.36,
      "end_seconds": 130.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "No, nothing, I've generally been healthy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.24,
      "end_seconds": 136.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.1,
      "end_seconds": 148.64,
      "duration_seconds": 11.54,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.71,
      "end_seconds": 151.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.86,
      "end_seconds": 154.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "No, never had any surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.91,
      "end_seconds": 160.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Bear with me, I need to finish this line in the notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.26,
      "end_seconds": 187.05,
      "duration_seconds": 15.79,
      "text": "That's saved, thanks for waiting. Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.42,
      "end_seconds": 190.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.15,
      "end_seconds": 195.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.01,
      "end_seconds": 197.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.49,
      "end_seconds": 200.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Take a breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.62,
      "end_seconds": 217.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Air entry is reduced on both sides with a prolonged breathing out phase."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.99,
      "end_seconds": 221.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Tell me if anything hurts as I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.92,
      "end_seconds": 241.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "There's some wheeze, and no swelling in the legs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.48,
      "end_seconds": 257.57,
      "duration_seconds": 11.09,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.95,
      "end_seconds": 260.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.87,
      "end_seconds": 271.6,
      "duration_seconds": 9.73,
      "text": "Putting it all together, my working impression is a flare-up of COPD. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.88,
      "end_seconds": 275.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.38,
      "end_seconds": 290.64,
      "duration_seconds": 14.26,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a flare-up of COPD do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had more breathlessness than usual, since Friday, and no fever or confusion."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.21,
      "end_seconds": 292.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.47,
      "end_seconds": 322.13,
      "duration_seconds": 28.66,
      "text": "Let's get a sputum culture, for productive cough. I'd like you to take doxycycline, 100 milligrams, twice a day, for five days. You take it by mouth. It's for chest infection. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. Please don't sit on it if you become more breathless or your lips turn blue. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.96,
      "end_seconds": 324.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.25,
      "end_seconds": 331.57,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Please come and see me in one week. Just to confirm, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.35,
      "end_seconds": 339.5,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "So, I take the doxycycline, 100 milligrams, twice a day and come back in one week. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.24,
      "end_seconds": 344.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.06,
      "end_seconds": 347.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Oh, no questions. Thank you."
    }
  ]
}